      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "caption": "Two strong definitions of one name is a hard link error.",
      "narration": "The first rule is simple. If two object files each define the same strong symbol, the linker stops with multiple definition of x.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Rule 1: strong vs strong",
