    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 11500,
      "caption": "COMMON merges to the largest size silently: a classic type-mismatch bug.",
      "narration": "With COMMON, same-named uninitialized globals are merged, and the largest size wins. A 40-byte buf and a 400-byte buf quietly share one object. GCC 10 defaults to fno-common.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "COMMON symbols",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "cm",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "c",
          "text": "/* a.c */ int buf[10];\n/* b.c */ int buf[100];\n/* -fcommon: one 400-byte buf */",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "fix",
